```go
package main

import "fmt"

func ReverseSlice(slice []int) {
    for i, j := 0, len(slice)-1; i < j; i, j = i+1, j-1 {
        slice[i], slice[j] = slice[j], slice[i]
    }
}

func main() {
    mySlice := []int{1, 2, 3, 4}
    fmt.Println("Before:", mySlice)
    ReverseSlice(mySlice)
    fmt.Println("After:", mySlice)
}
```

This script defines a `ReverseSlice` function that reverses the elements in a slice. It uses two pointers (`i` and `j`) to swap elements from start to end until they meet or pass each other, effectively reversing the entire slice in place without needing any additional data structures.

